      "message": "I\u0027m wondering if there is a better way to refactor it.\nE.g.\n```\npreBaseRunner()\nbaseRunner.run(notifier)\npostBaseRunner()\n\nor \n\nmonitorThreadLeakForTask(notifier: RunNotifier, task: Runnable) {\n  if (!shouldThreadLeakFailTest) {\n            task()\n            return\n  }\n  // Dump threads as a baseline to monitor thread leaks.\n   val threadCountsBeforeTest \u003d getAllThreadNameCounts()\n   task()\n   checkThreadLeak(notifier, threadCountsBeforeTest)\n}\n\nif so maybe we can \nmonitorThreadLeakForTask(notifier, () -\u003e baseRunner.run())\n\nand maybe also chain your function into:\nmonitorDefaultNetworkForTask(notifier, () -\u003e \n    monitorThreadLeakForTask(notifier, () -\u003e \n        baseRunner.run()))\n```\n\nI think the nesting is ugly but not that bad. WDYT?",
